{"id": "EUVD-2026-80550", "enisaUuid": "de4fbbdb-80f7-396d-9985-05811a8b5fc6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbatman-adv: mcast: linearize skbuff for packet generation\n\nbatadv_mcast_forw_packet() and batadv_mcast_forw_scrape() is not only\ncalled (indirectly) by the unsharing+linearizing batadv_recv_mcast_packet()\nhandler. When it is called (indirectly) by batadv_mcast_forw_mcsend() then\nit will be unshared but not linearized. The SKB_LINEAR_ASSERT() can\ntherefore cause a fatal BUG().\n\nThe linearization should happen during the expansion of the head because\nthe scrape function can be hit already during the initial\nbatadv_mcast_forw_mode() selection code:\n\n* batadv_interface_tx\n* batadv_mcast_forw_mode\n* batadv_mcast_forw_mode_by_count()\n* batadv_mcast_forw_push()\n  -> calls batadv_mcast_forw_expand_head() before everything else\n* batadv_mcast_forw_push_tvlvs()\n* batadv_mcast_forw_push_dests()\n* batadv_mcast_forw_push_adjust_padding()\n* batadv_mcast_forw_scrape()", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:55:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9603e0a7cb5e0cddc6b23af153cf7daafc5c55e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c32e5e25c41201c8c3b796a4ab2c45103187091e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2879177539e3ece483a8e5406970373698e9a6c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a30a59e2660afd03c975f1b8eae6a2301161197"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3h9h-h4qr-r799", "CVE-2026-89950"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "23d87c27-4157-3f43-9be8-592beb3519e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "90039133221e33964ccb4a536dad7eb0a372fff7 <a9603e0a7cb5e0cddc6b23af153cf7daafc5c55e"}, {"id": "301e2dc6-1de8-3f97-bfab-2e6f477bb527", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "32e640da-793f-3ded-b7e9-31cda396ad91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "90039133221e33964ccb4a536dad7eb0a372fff7 <c32e5e25c41201c8c3b796a4ab2c45103187091e"}, {"id": "3b2ea229-7def-3688-ab1a-958b8ece1d12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "90039133221e33964ccb4a536dad7eb0a372fff7 <6a30a59e2660afd03c975f1b8eae6a2301161197"}, {"id": "5ea603e8-d2e4-31bd-8c4c-247462fe656e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6f9fe0c7-ea0b-327c-ac22-d99da6fa5b6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "781704b8-f0df-3ef4-9561-2ae1f83f020e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c852f806-a276-3cb5-8d28-5fa97982e1b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "cfe7aa5a-cb4c-3c4b-8f0b-cbfd5cbb209a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "90039133221e33964ccb4a536dad7eb0a372fff7 <2879177539e3ece483a8e5406970373698e9a6c5"}, {"id": "e638c3c8-2e0f-3887-b6ea-f9d08ca37874", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c73b289c-9c36-30ea-8392-2a4f6c728835", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}